1
00:00:00,233 --> 00:00:00,733
Hello大家好
Hi everyone

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,066
前两天群里有个人丢了问题
A couple of days ago, someone in a group chat threw out a question

3
00:00:04,433 --> 00:00:05,933
AI都能做题了
AI can already solve math problems

4
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:08,000
那么还要数学系干什么呢
so what's the point of a math department

5
00:00:08,766 --> 00:00:11,833
这件事的起因是OpenAI一次放出了近400
It started when OpenAI released nearly 400

6
00:00:11,833 --> 00:00:14,833
项数学成果 有的数学家看完之后觉得
math results at once, and one mathematician said

7
00:00:15,066 --> 00:00:17,800
这些东西已经够他消化好多年了
there was enough there for him to digest for years

8
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:20,033
群里的反应其实很分裂
The group was pretty divided

9
00:00:20,033 --> 00:00:21,466
有一半人欢呼
Half of them were cheering

10
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,900
哇 又能少写一些代码了
wow, even less code to write

11
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:25,833
另一半人会担心
The other half were worried

12
00:00:25,933 --> 00:00:27,666
轮到我被迭代了
now it's my turn to be replaced

13
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:29,733
我听着那句话看了很久
I stared at that line for a long time

14
00:00:29,733 --> 00:00:31,866
觉得他问的不是数学
and felt it wasn't really about math

15
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:32,833
他问的是
What it's really asking is

16
00:00:32,833 --> 00:00:35,100
如果有一样东西变强了
when something gets more powerful

17
00:00:35,133 --> 00:00:38,966
那么原来靠这件东西吃饭的人会去哪呢
where do the people who made a living from it go

18
00:00:39,833 --> 00:00:40,866
按照这个问法
Framed that way

19
00:00:40,866 --> 00:00:42,833
答案好像只剩无处可去
the only answer seems to be nowhere

20
00:00:43,100 --> 00:00:44,700
但我翻了一晚上资料
But after a whole night of reading up

21
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:47,266
发现发生的这件事和这个问法
I found that what's actually happening and that question

22
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:48,333
其实离得很远
are pretty far apart

23
00:00:48,733 --> 00:00:50,266
这里是像素呼吸
This is Pixel Breath

24
00:00:50,366 --> 00:00:51,900
今天我们一起聊一聊
Today let's talk about

25
00:00:52,066 --> 00:00:53,466
当AI越来越强
as AI gets stronger

26
00:00:53,600 --> 00:00:55,333
什么东西会变得值钱呢
what becomes more valuable

27
00:00:55,500 --> 00:00:56,933
首先我想跟大家承认的是
First, I'll admit

28
00:00:57,133 --> 00:00:59,266
这个担心真的没什么问题
this worry is totally fair

29
00:00:59,766 --> 00:01:01,466
它的背后有一个默认推理
Behind it is an unspoken assumption

30
00:01:01,700 --> 00:01:03,166
一个东西便宜了
when something gets cheaper

31
00:01:03,233 --> 00:01:06,300
那么和它有关的一切东西都跟着不值钱
everything connected to it loses value too

32
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:08,333
这个推理通常是对的
That reasoning is usually right

33
00:01:08,466 --> 00:01:10,300
同样一个东西如果有好几家做
If several shops sell the same thing

34
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:12,200
那么一家降价
and one cuts its price

35
00:01:12,266 --> 00:01:13,400
别家就跟着降
the others follow

36
00:01:13,533 --> 00:01:15,800
整条街都不赚钱
and nobody on the street makes money

37
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:16,900
这叫替代
That's called substitution

38
00:01:16,900 --> 00:01:19,833
你和那件东西干的其实是一件事
You and that thing are doing the same job

39
00:01:20,166 --> 00:01:22,000
比如一条卖衣服的街
Say there's a street of clothing shops

40
00:01:22,033 --> 00:01:24,600
你卖30 那么我卖50
you sell for 30 and I sell for 50

41
00:01:25,033 --> 00:01:27,433
我一定在价格上其实是不占优势的
then I'm clearly losing on price

42
00:01:27,466 --> 00:01:29,000
那我也要降价
so I have to cut my price too

43
00:01:29,033 --> 00:01:33,933
那降着降着其实整条街都不太能有很好的收益
and as prices keep falling, nobody on the street does well

44
00:01:34,166 --> 00:01:36,466
如果是两件事只是搭在一起用
But if they're two different things that just get used together

45
00:01:36,466 --> 00:01:38,100
那么结论会反过来
the conclusion flips

46
00:01:38,133 --> 00:01:39,966
一个便宜 那么另一个就贵
when one gets cheaper, the other gets pricier

47
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:44,800
老家的县城 高铁通了从省城回去需要40分钟
Back in my hometown, high-speed rail made it 40 minutes from the provincial capital

48
00:01:44,833 --> 00:01:46,866
按理路程更便宜了
In theory, getting there got cheaper

49
00:01:46,933 --> 00:01:49,066
小城里的东西也应该更便宜
so things in a small town should get cheaper too

50
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:51,633
可是县城的酒店会先涨价
But the county's hotels raised prices first

51
00:01:51,766 --> 00:01:54,666
每个周末订房得提前两天去预订
On weekends you have to book two days ahead

52
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:58,033
我还专门查了资料看看是不是错觉
I even looked into it to see if I was imagining things

53
00:01:58,100 --> 00:01:59,266
有研究计算过
One study ran the numbers

54
00:01:59,433 --> 00:02:03,033
如果沿线城市的旅游人数涨了百分之18点5
tourist numbers in cities along the line rose 18.5%

55
00:02:03,033 --> 00:02:05,433
那么旅游收入会涨百分之25
and tourism revenue rose 25%

56
00:02:05,466 --> 00:02:08,500
另一个团队去算了178个城市
Another team looked at 178 cities

57
00:02:08,733 --> 00:02:10,766
平均收入涨了百分之12
and found revenue up 12% on average

58
00:02:10,800 --> 00:02:13,400
高铁没有让县城变得更便宜
High-speed rail didn't make the county cheaper

59
00:02:13,433 --> 00:02:15,966
反而它却把需求都挤进了县城
instead it squeezed demand into the county

60
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,033
当高铁能通往这个县城
Once high-speed rail reaches a county

61
00:02:18,066 --> 00:02:20,933
那么这里的人流量就会越变越大
more and more people start coming

62
00:02:20,933 --> 00:02:22,266
当人流量多了
and with more people

63
00:02:22,300 --> 00:02:24,000
这些需求也被带了进来
all that demand comes with them

64
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:25,700
更狠的一个是光伏
An even more extreme case is solar

65
00:02:25,700 --> 00:02:27,966
它的组件2022年底
At the end of 2022, solar modules

66
00:02:27,966 --> 00:02:30,366
平均下来两块一毛钱一瓦
averaged 2.1 yuan per watt

67
00:02:30,366 --> 00:02:32,200
2025年3月份
By March 2025

68
00:02:32,233 --> 00:02:33,833
光伏越来越轻松
going solar should be getting easier

69
00:02:34,266 --> 00:02:36,600
可国际能源署的数据却不是这样的
But the International Energy Agency's data says otherwise

70
00:02:36,633 --> 00:02:40,633
过去五年电网用的电缆和变压器的价格几乎翻倍
Over the past five years, grid cables and transformers nearly doubled in price

71
00:02:40,633 --> 00:02:40,800
过去五年电网用的电缆和变压器的价格几乎翻倍
Over the past five years, grid cables and transformers nearly doubled in price

72
00:02:40,833 --> 00:02:43,666
变压器的交期从几个月变成两三年
Transformer lead times went from a few months to two or three years

73
00:02:44,066 --> 00:02:46,200
光伏这里的板子变便宜了
Solar panels got cheaper

74
00:02:46,200 --> 00:02:49,266
但是把电送出去这件事就变贵了
but getting the power out got more expensive

75
00:02:49,666 --> 00:02:50,966
翻译一下
Put simply

76
00:02:50,966 --> 00:02:52,500
如果一个东西降价
when one thing gets cheaper

77
00:02:52,533 --> 00:02:55,033
那么不会让全世界都变便宜
it doesn't make the whole world cheaper

78
00:02:55,033 --> 00:02:56,933
它会把需求挤到一旁
it pushes demand onto whatever sits next to it

79
00:02:57,433 --> 00:02:59,333
那么如果AI被降价之后
So once AI gets cheaper

80
00:02:59,333 --> 00:03:01,333
被挤的是哪一样东西呢
what gets squeezed

81
00:03:01,566 --> 00:03:03,566
一百年前 电也这么没用过
A hundred years ago, electricity seemed just as useless

82
00:03:03,700 --> 00:03:05,333
爱迪生点亮了电灯
Edison lit up the light bulb

83
00:03:05,866 --> 00:03:08,933
1882年 纽约珍珠街的电厂才供电
In 1882, New York's Pearl Street Station started supplying power

84
00:03:09,133 --> 00:03:10,733
那会儿的工程师就明白
Engineers back then already knew

85
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,500
电会改掉工厂
electricity would transform factories

86
00:03:12,633 --> 00:03:14,300
可接下来的30年
But for the next 30 years

87
00:03:14,466 --> 00:03:16,800
工厂的生产效率几乎没有怎么动
factory productivity barely moved

88
00:03:17,366 --> 00:03:19,766
电便宜了 机器也换了
Power got cheaper, the machines were replaced

89
00:03:19,966 --> 00:03:21,933
为什么活还没有变快呢
so why wasn't work getting any faster

90
00:03:22,366 --> 00:03:25,033
为什么我们的效率依然没有增加呢
why was productivity still flat

91
00:03:25,633 --> 00:03:26,866
十九世纪的工厂
A 19th-century factory

92
00:03:26,866 --> 00:03:28,233
整体只依靠一根总轴
ran entirely on a single line shaft

93
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:31,666
水轮或蒸汽机都在工厂外面去转
A water wheel or steam engine turned outside the building

94
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,433
带动厂房顶上的那条长轴
driving a long shaft along the ceiling

95
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:36,800
轴上挂了一圈皮带
with belts hung all along it

96
00:03:37,066 --> 00:03:39,566
皮带垂下来连着一台又一台的机器
and the belts dropped down to drive machine after machine

97
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:41,800
这个是之前的死规矩
That was the iron rule back then

98
00:03:41,933 --> 00:03:44,633
所有机器都会围着这根总轴转
every machine had to sit around that shaft

99
00:03:45,033 --> 00:03:47,100
车间只能按照动力去排
So the floor was laid out by power

100
00:03:47,366 --> 00:03:49,033
不能按照工序去排
not by the order of the work

101
00:03:50,033 --> 00:03:51,566
当电走入人们的生活
When electricity came along

102
00:03:51,766 --> 00:03:53,200
很多工厂干了什么
what did a lot of factories do

103
00:03:53,766 --> 00:03:57,366
首先 把外面的蒸汽机换成一个特别大的电动机
They swapped the steam engine outside for one huge electric motor

104
00:03:57,500 --> 00:04:00,033
总轴还在 皮带也没变
The shaft stayed, the belts stayed

105
00:04:00,266 --> 00:04:02,833
机器还是要围着那根总轴去转
and the machines still had to sit around the shaft

106
00:04:02,933 --> 00:04:04,433
这叫成组驱动
This is called group drive

107
00:04:04,666 --> 00:04:07,733
而车间依然还是原来的那套运行规则
but the floor still ran by the old rules

108
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,166
总轴一开 全厂都转
Start the shaft and the whole plant turns

109
00:04:10,633 --> 00:04:13,500
长轴上摩擦消耗的力比干活的还多
Friction along the shaft ate more power than the actual work

110
00:04:14,233 --> 00:04:15,666
哪怕只想开一台
even if you only want one machine running

111
00:04:15,666 --> 00:04:16,800
机器只能摆两排
Machines could only go in two rows

112
00:04:17,066 --> 00:04:19,733
物料从这头搬过去再运回来
Materials got hauled across and then hauled back again

113
00:04:20,266 --> 00:04:21,400
吃到电的好处
To really get the benefits of electricity

114
00:04:21,566 --> 00:04:23,900
那么就需要把整个工厂拆掉重建
you had to tear the factory down and rebuild it

115
00:04:23,933 --> 00:04:26,433
每个机器配一个小电机
Give every machine its own small motor

116
00:04:26,733 --> 00:04:28,133
想开哪台就开哪台
and run whichever one you want

117
00:04:28,266 --> 00:04:31,366
并且车间也不用围着这一根总轴去转
The floor no longer had to revolve around the shaft

118
00:04:31,900 --> 00:04:33,333
按照工序进行排布
it could be laid out in the order of the work

119
00:04:33,366 --> 00:04:35,000
物料也从一头进
Materials go in one end

120
00:04:35,133 --> 00:04:36,100
从另一头出
and out the other

121
00:04:36,700 --> 00:04:38,100
时间花了多久呢
How long did that take

122
00:04:38,566 --> 00:04:40,833
1882年已经开始了供电
Power was available from 1882

123
00:04:40,966 --> 00:04:44,666
直到1920年代才真正开始进行工厂的迭代
but factories didn't really transform until the 1920s

124
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:46,100
将近40年
Nearly 40 years

125
00:04:46,566 --> 00:04:47,833
那这40年不是没电
Those 40 years weren't for lack of power

126
00:04:47,933 --> 00:04:49,400
而是大家都不敢拆
people just didn't dare tear things down

127
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:52,033
厂房是钱 总轴也是钱
The building cost money, the shaft cost money

128
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:55,633
停产重排更是一些资金的消耗
and shutting down to rearrange cost even more

129
00:04:55,800 --> 00:04:58,600
一直到1920年代 投资环境变好了
Only in the 1920s, when the investment climate improved

130
00:04:58,600 --> 00:05:01,533
才有人整片的重新盖起新的厂房
did people start building whole new factories

131
00:05:02,133 --> 00:05:05,300
电作为工厂动力的份额在1919年的时候
Electricity's share of factory power in 1919

132
00:05:05,600 --> 00:05:08,733
只刚过一半 在1929年接近八成
was just over half, and by 1929 it was nearly 80%

133
00:05:08,966 --> 00:05:13,433
制造业生产增速1920年代远超之前20年
Manufacturing productivity growth in the 1920s far outpaced the previous 20 years

134
00:05:13,433 --> 00:05:16,166
研究这一段的经济学家估算
Economic historians who study this period estimate

135
00:05:16,600 --> 00:05:20,433
其中至少一半能归结到拆总轴这件事情上
at least half of that came from getting rid of the line shaft

136
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:24,600
翻译一下 让工厂变快的是重构整个厂房
Put simply, what made factories faster was redesigning the whole plant

137
00:05:24,766 --> 00:05:27,166
电只是让重构变得更划算
electricity just made the redesign worth it

138
00:05:27,433 --> 00:05:29,666
电变便宜之后 跟着变贵的不是电
Once electricity got cheaper, what got expensive wasn't electricity

139
00:05:29,866 --> 00:05:32,033
而是怎么知道重构的那批人
it was the people who knew how to redesign

140
00:05:32,233 --> 00:05:33,833
和愿意停产重构的时间
and the time to shut down and rebuild

141
00:05:34,533 --> 00:05:36,033
那么难点在哪里呢
So where's the hard part

142
00:05:36,766 --> 00:05:38,266
技术很早就到位了
The technology was ready early on

143
00:05:38,266 --> 00:05:40,866
重构却不在大家的采购清单上
but redesign wasn't on anyone's shopping list

144
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:42,866
没有报价 没有供应商
No quotes, no suppliers

145
00:05:42,900 --> 00:05:45,933
没有人能给你开一张换一种排法的发票
no one can invoice you for "a new layout"

146
00:05:45,933 --> 00:05:48,166
这40年卡的就是这个
That's what held things up for 40 years

147
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,033
我们回到AI
Now back to AI

148
00:05:50,200 --> 00:05:52,300
用同一套看法再去看一遍
Let's look at it the same way

149
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:55,600
AI变便宜变的是做那件事
What AI makes cheap is the doing

150
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:58,366
写一段文字 画一张画
writing a passage, drawing a picture

151
00:05:58,566 --> 00:06:00,200
当做变便宜了
Once doing gets cheap

152
00:06:00,266 --> 00:06:01,500
需求就被挤到一边
demand gets pushed to the side

153
00:06:01,666 --> 00:06:03,833
我的判断是挤到看上
My take is it gets pushed onto checking

154
00:06:04,333 --> 00:06:06,866
AI一天可以写出你之前一周写的量
AI can write in a day what used to take you a week

155
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:09,166
但你要看的量也跟着上涨
but the amount you have to review goes up too

156
00:06:09,333 --> 00:06:12,533
它写的越多 你越得需要逐条去检验
The more it writes, the more you have to check line by line

157
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:14,233
那么去检验什么呢
Check for what

158
00:06:14,433 --> 00:06:15,966
检验它有没有编数据
Whether it made up data

159
00:06:16,033 --> 00:06:17,266
有没有产生幻觉
whether it hallucinated

160
00:06:17,400 --> 00:06:20,933
有没有出现一些违反现实的一些反例
whether anything in it contradicts reality

161
00:06:21,433 --> 00:06:23,366
这句结论能不能落到账上呢
and whether the conclusion actually holds up

162
00:06:23,366 --> 00:06:25,566
以前会不那么较真
We didn't use to be this picky

163
00:06:25,700 --> 00:06:29,700
因为自己写的大概都知道哪个地方我没有去查
because when I wrote it myself, I knew where I hadn't checked

164
00:06:29,733 --> 00:06:33,700
数据 或者哪个地方我去进行了一些数据的构造
the data, or where I'd made up some numbers

165
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,800
但现在虚的地方是
But now the weak spots

166
00:06:35,800 --> 00:06:36,733
AI替我留的
are ones AI left for me

167
00:06:36,966 --> 00:06:39,100
会写现在已经不是很稀缺
Being able to write isn't scarce anymore

168
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:42,100
稀缺的是如何能看出哪个部分不对
what's scarce is spotting which part is wrong

169
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:44,266
一件东西变便宜
If something gets cheaper

170
00:06:44,433 --> 00:06:46,833
那么旁边没有配套的稀缺环节
and there's nothing scarce that goes with it

171
00:06:46,966 --> 00:06:48,600
那就只是单纯变便宜
then it's simply cheaper, nothing more

172
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,533
比如当盐降价了
Say salt gets cheaper

173
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:54,900
没有人会因为想去多吃一点盐而去学做饭
nobody learns to cook just to eat more salt

174
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:58,900
AI也一样 用它的时候身边没有别的东西变得
Same with AI: if nothing around you gets

175
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:00,800
紧张 那你就是纯省钱
tight when you use it, you're just saving money

176
00:07:00,800 --> 00:07:02,400
我自己的感受是
My own sense is

177
00:07:02,533 --> 00:07:04,666
现在的紧张是相信这件事
what's tight now is trust

178
00:07:04,666 --> 00:07:06,500
以前当我写完文章
Before, when I finished an article

179
00:07:06,566 --> 00:07:07,700
可以直接发出去
I could just publish it

180
00:07:08,033 --> 00:07:11,066
因为文章是我一个字一个字敲出来的
because I'd typed every word myself

181
00:07:11,066 --> 00:07:13,300
但现在 AI写完之后
But now, after AI writes it

182
00:07:13,400 --> 00:07:15,266
我需要这儿看一下那儿看一下
I have to check here and check there

183
00:07:15,633 --> 00:07:17,400
并且去验证其中的例子
and verify the examples in it

184
00:07:17,433 --> 00:07:19,766
这些就是眼下最贵的地方
That's the most expensive part right now

185
00:07:20,333 --> 00:07:21,433
这周我需要找一个时间
This week I'm going to set aside some time

186
00:07:21,433 --> 00:07:23,466
去把AI帮我写过的文章
to take the articles AI wrote for me

187
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:24,533
以及干过的事
and the work it's done

188
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:26,866
仔仔细细地剖析一遍
and go through them carefully

189
00:07:26,866 --> 00:07:28,433
它到底哪里不行
to see where it falls short

190
00:07:28,433 --> 00:07:31,033
到底哪里是真正可以替代我的地方
and where it can truly replace me

191
00:07:31,633 --> 00:07:32,166
回到开头
Back to where we started

192
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:35,433
那现在还需要数学系和这些数学专家干什么
so do we still need math departments and mathematicians

193
00:07:36,166 --> 00:07:37,366
我的答案变了一点
My answer has changed a bit

194
00:07:37,366 --> 00:07:40,833
如果AI一次真的能产出几百项成果
If AI really can produce hundreds of results at once

195
00:07:40,833 --> 00:07:43,366
那么最先不够用的是这些
what runs short first is

196
00:07:43,400 --> 00:07:46,800
能判断这些成果是否用到我们生活中的专家
experts who can judge whether those results apply to real life

197
00:07:47,433 --> 00:07:50,366
上期我们说了 AI越便宜你用的越多
Last time we said the cheaper AI gets, the more you use it

198
00:07:50,966 --> 00:07:52,466
现在我要补后半句
Now here's the second half

199
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:53,800
当你用的越多
The more you use it

200
00:07:54,133 --> 00:07:56,233
越需要一个能说这条不对的人
the more you need someone who can say "this is wrong"

201
00:07:56,233 --> 00:07:58,333
那个人现在还挺贵的
And that person is still pretty expensive

202
00:07:58,333 --> 00:07:59,733
我们下期聊
See you next time
